>Tarp shelter quick card
Choose safe drained ground clear of falling branches, flood routes and rockfall.
Use sound supports and a low ridgeline. Centre the tarp, stake the corners and direct runoff away from your mat. Keep airflow and a clear exit. Insulate underneath yourself. Use no flame or stove under the shelter. Move if supports fail or water rises.

`[Pitching an A-frame tarp`:/page/shelter/tarp.mu]

